Niki Agent
==========

Niki Agent is an independent terminal coding agent. The agent loop, the
terminal UI, and the ACP integration live in this repository; nothing imports an
upstream agent distribution at runtime.

The MIT license at the repository root applies to Niki Agent.

Vendored components
-------------------

Two directories are copies of MIT-licensed software developed by LangChain, Inc.,
taken from the Deep Agents project (https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents):

  * `libs/code/niki_agent/sdk/` — the `deepagents` package, version 0.7.21.
  * `libs/code/niki_agent/acp_sdk/` — the `deepagents-acp` package, version
    0.0.12.

Each directory carries a `PROVENANCE.md` naming the upstream version, the commit
it was copied from, and the mechanical changes made to the copy, alongside a
`LICENSE` file with the upstream notice reproduced verbatim:

    MIT License
    Copyright (c) LangChain, Inc.

The full upstream license text is also preserved at
`libs/code/niki_agent/sdk/LICENSE` and `libs/code/niki_agent/acp_sdk/LICENSE`.

Third-party components
----------------------

Niki Agent depends on third-party packages including Textual, Rich, LangChain,
and LangGraph. Their licenses apply unchanged; see `libs/code/pyproject.toml`
for the dependency list.
